<b>EQ NOTES:</b>

Rumor (from a wiz) has it that wearing two of *anything* does nothing different 
aside from 2x the effect of wearing one.  For example, coiled serpents or purple
gloves may give no bonus for having a complete set.

Axl's told me that regen is a random +-x%, so that an item with +4 sp regen
may actually appear to be +3-6 regen, for example.  This explains the
seemingly contradictory regen stats often argued about on sales channel.
I've tried to hit on the true regen value in this list, but ranges still do
exist and the info I list may not be entirely accurate.

Also, Malack added:

   Btw i tested Axl's theory about the +/- factor and found it
   to be pretty accurate--ex:  rainbow cloak is +3-5, but in 20 or so tries i
   never had a +4.  I think what is done is the base factor is +4, but a plus
   or minus 1 is always added to the base factor giving a result of either 
   +3 or +5.



